om2 diag bce
note bce fixture kept: no check here is erasable, so om2 bce must compile to the same bytes as om2: an
note unsized view (every index checked), a text (kind 5), a uint counter (the index is a converted
note temporary), a count that is a value, a while loop with its own counter, a count of 0 and an unrolled
note loop (constant indices, no run-time check either way). a[i] = i, so the exit is
note 6 + 6 + 6 + 3 + 6 + 0 + 6 = 33.
text t "abcdefgh"
fn sv a view ulong * to ulong
s = ulong 0
for i ulong 4
s = add s get a i
end
ret s
end
fn main to int
a = new ulong 8 1
z = ulong 0
while lt z 8
put a z z
z = add z 1
end
s = sv a
for i ulong 3
s = add s ulong sub get t i 96
end
for i uint 4
s = add s get a ulong i
end
n = ulong 3
for i ulong n
s = add s get a i
end
k = ulong 0
while lt k 4
s = add s get a k
k = add k 1
end
for i ulong 0
s = add s get a i
end
for i ulong 4 unroll
s = add s get a i
end
ret int s
end
